Issue #378 review — DONE

**Changes requested.** This is a static review of chunk 1; I did not run tests or phone UAT. I found no direct path that builds `LocalLog.words` text while Detailed log is Off, or sends that text to logcat or telemetry. The switch race below can, however, leave the file gate On after the UI reports Off.

1. **BLOCKING · REPRODUCIBLE** — [DeveloperSwitches.kt:90](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DeveloperSwitches.kt:90): An On request can suspend in DataStore, letting a later Off finish first. When On resumes, it recreates the flag; the sequence check suppresses only its UI update. Dictated words can then be written while the page says Off. Serialize the *entire* suspend operation with a mutex or request channel, including cold-start repair, and publish state only after storage and flag agree. Add a test that holds On until Off has completed, then releases it; the current test releases On before checking Off.

2. **BLOCKING · REPRODUCIBLE** — [AudioCaptureService.kt:518](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/AudioCaptureService.kt:518), [AudioCaptureService.kt:810](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/AudioCaptureService.kt:810): Route start, recording stop, ending, and other capture lines still use plain `DebugLogger`, so their file entries have `take=-`. Keep the take's `TakeLog` on `CaptureSession` and use it for every take-scoped capture line. Pass the take log through take-specific polish fallback warnings too. Add a test covering start, route, stop, and fallback lines for one ID.

3. **NON-BLOCKING · REPRODUCIBLE** — [DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:902](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:902): A speech request that throws after its take ends logs through the mutable `take` field. If another take has begun, that warning gets the new ID. Capture the original `TakeContext` outside the `try`, use its log in the catch block, and pass it into `failFromWorker`; use no ID if that context is unavailable.

4. **NON-BLOCKING · REPRODUCIBLE** — [DeveloperLogs.kt:46](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DeveloperLogs.kt:46): Two concurrent adb pulls can race. The second export deletes the first ZIP after its future completes but before [openFile](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DeveloperLogProvider.kt:47) opens it. Keep each ZIP until its own descriptor is open; remove only abandoned files, and make timeout cleanup target its own export.

5. **NON-BLOCKING · REPRODUCIBLE** — [DeveloperLogProvider.kt:56](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DeveloperLogProvider.kt:56): `call()` checks shell UID but omits the plan’s explicit DUMP check. `getType()` has neither check. Add one `requireShellAndDump()` helper and call it first in every provider entry. The current UID check prevents an ordinary app from using `call()`; this finding is a missing required gate, not a demonstrated content leak.

6. **NON-BLOCKING · REPRODUCIBLE** — [wispr_eyes.py:3914](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/uat/wispr_eyes.py:3914): `pull_log` validates the ZIP header and `device.txt`, but can accept a corrupt log entry. Call `ZipFile.testzip()` before `os.replace` and reject any named bad entry.

